course: dictionary
lesson: 10728
title: Uphill: a direction and a hard task
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Walking uphill, people lean forward to keep their weight over their feet.» Uphill tells you the direction: going up a slope, towards the top of a hill. The lean is a clue, because you feel the ground rising under you.
explain: Uphill can also describe something hard. «An uphill struggle» or «an uphill battle» is a task that takes a lot of effort, where you must keep pushing against difficulty. Ask yourself: is the sentence about a slope, or about something hard? The words around it give the clue.
explain: «Canals cannot run uphill, so engineers built locks» shows uphill in its literal sense. Water flows downhill, so a boat needs a lock to go up or down. Downhill is the opposite of uphill.
fact: Uphill means going up a slope, towards the top of a hill.
fact: An uphill task or battle is something hard that takes a lot of effort.
fact: The opposite of uphill is downhill.
fact: «Uphill» can be an adverb or an adjective, as in «walk uphill» and «an uphill climb».
fact: Rivers flow downhill, not uphill, so water runs down to the sea.
exercise: «Walking uphill, people lean forward to keep their weight over their feet.» What does uphill mean here? | Running very fast on a road | *Going up a slope towards the top of a hill | Sitting still on flat ground | Going down a slope to the bottom
exercise: «The training was an uphill struggle, but Maya never gave up.» What does uphill mean in this sentence? | *Something hard that takes a lot of effort | Wet and muddy | A steep road with cars on it | Easy and fun
exercise: Which word is the opposite of uphill? | Uphill again | Sideways | *Downhill | Upstairs
test: «Canals cannot run uphill, so engineers built locks.» What is the job of the locks? | Keep the boats still in the water | *Lift a boat up or let it down | Pump water uphill with a motor | Make the canal shallow
test: «Some stations pump water uphill at night and let it run down later, like a giant battery.» What does uphill mean here? | Something hard to finish | Very fast | Going down to the sea | *Going up towards higher ground
exam: Which sentence uses uphill to mean something hard? | *«Winning the chess tournament was an uphill battle.» | «The toy is marked 3+ for ages 3 and up.» | «Walkers climbed uphill slowly.» | «The river flows downhill to the sea.»
